hydra
Usage: hydra -l USER -P LIST [-s PORT] TARGET SERVICE

Online login brute-forcer: it tries username/password pairs against a live
service -- ssh, http, ftp and many more -- and reports what worked. Online
means loud and rate-limited; keep the thread count low to stay quiet.

	-l USER / -L FILE   one username / a list of them
	-p PASS / -P FILE   one password / a wordlist
	-s PORT             the service port
	-t N                N parallel tries (lower = quieter)
	-f                  stop at the first valid login
	-V                  show every attempt
	-o FILE             write found logins to a file

Only against a service you own or are authorised to test.

See also: john, nmap
